{"content":[{"c":["BAAL-ZEPHON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Area opposite the Israelites’ encampment just before they crossed the Red Sea (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.14.2,9","r":"Exod.14.2,9","rawR":"Exod.14.2,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.14.2,9","value":"Exod.14.2,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 14:2, 9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.7","r":"Num.33.7","rawR":"Num.33.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.7","value":"Num.33.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 33:7"},"). The exact location of Baal-zephon is unknown but probably was in northeast Egypt. The name means “lord of the north,” and a shrine to a Semitic deity was presumably located there. The god Baal-zephon is mentioned in Ugaritic, Egyptian, and Phoenician writings as a sea and storm god."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BaalZephon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 14:2, 9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.14.2,9","rawQueryValue":"Exod.14.2,9","sourceRefExact":"Exod.14.2,9"},{"anchorText":"Nm 33:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.7","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.7","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"fa9a23e88b2a1fc7967cc5b644853902cf07f9bc9b8c04095911c1d464ec3446","sourceItemName":"BaalZephon","sourceItemOrder":23,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BaalZephon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Baal-Zephon","title":"Baal-Zephon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}